	(text "MAIZE PHASE 5 CONTROLLER  —  read this before believing a wire\nAssumptions, because the gate, pilot, and sensor terminals are still unmeasured:\n1. Coil drivers are 24 V DC, about 0.5 A each. An AC coil does not belong on this board.\n2. Opening power is a relay contact. It drops if the processor stops kicking the watchdog,\n   the enable key is open, the mode is OFF, or STOP is pressed.\n3. Close-coil force jumpers stay OPEN until a double-acting actuator is proven.\n   Spring-return valves must leave those jumpers empty. Loss of 24 V then lets the spring close.\n4. Sensor inputs are dry contacts. The board puts about 5 mA through a closed contact.\n5. Hornet DE-9 follows the archived IGM402 map: 9 = data B (+), 6 = data A (-), 4 = isolated reference.\n   Pin 2 (gauge 20-28 V) is not connected. Relay pins 1, 5, 7 are brought out and are not a filament proof.\n6. Cold-ready, filament-off, and pump-ready are contact landings waiting for the real measurement.\n7. The scroll pump, Cryo-Torr, and CTI compressor are not powered or started by this board.\n8. Logic input is 9-12 V at J_LOGIC. Do not also power the Uno from USB.\n9. UART 7-bit I2C address is 0x48 (A1 and A0 tied to 3.3 V). Baud is a firmware choice after the Hornet manual matches.\n10. Active-low inputs: a closed contact reads as true, same idea as the phase 1 buttons."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.0 2140.0 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "3ffa14e2-cc6c-4083-b8b7-041a834c7292")
	)
	(text "POWER  9-12 V logic, separate 24 V coils. Gauge 24 V stays on the Hornet supply."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.0 1980.0 0)
		(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "adf075f1-63eb-44ec-b79a-ba268a9f2928")
	)
